WEBVTT

00:40.510 --> 00:49.270
TONIKAWA

00:40.510 --> 00:49.270
TONIKAWA

01:31.020 --> 01:37.030
<b>Episode 7      An Expanding World</b>

01:35.800 --> 01:38.620
It sure is hot, darling.

01:39.080 --> 01:40.740
Sure is.

01:41.280 --> 01:45.180
It was pouring non-stop after we 
got back from the hot spring,

01:45.180 --> 01:47.930
but now it's like summer kicked 
into high gear all of a sudden.

01:47.930 --> 01:49.750
You've got that right.

01:50.000 --> 01:53.680
That talk about it being a 
cooler summer this year...

01:53.680 --> 01:56.520
Where did it even come from?

01:56.520 --> 02:00.010
Well, the news always tends 
to prop up theories like that.

02:00.450 --> 02:05.690
Y'know, there's something I've only 
noticed now that summer's started.

02:05.690 --> 02:07.200
The AC in this room...

02:09.150 --> 02:11.900
does not work at all.

02:11.900 --> 02:14.650
It definitely does not.

02:15.350 --> 02:17.680
I can't focus on work when it's this hot,

02:17.680 --> 02:19.660
and I doubt it's good for us or Toast!

02:19.660 --> 02:22.230
I'm gonna go buy an air conditioner!

02:23.290 --> 02:26.670
So, is it okay if we install a new 
air conditioner in that building?

02:26.670 --> 02:29.670
It's not a problem, but...

02:30.060 --> 02:34.950
I mean, most of the time, you won't actually 
have your AC until two weeks after buying it.

02:35.670 --> 02:37.570
B-But why?!

02:38.110 --> 02:42.180
I mean, they need to be installed, right?

02:42.180 --> 02:42.720
<b>July 17</b>

02:42.180 --> 02:43.350
<b>July 11</b>

02:42.180 --> 02:43.640
<b>July 16</b>

02:42.180 --> 02:44.140
<b>July 10</b>

02:42.180 --> 02:44.720
<b>July 15</b>

02:42.180 --> 02:45.060
<b>July 9</b>

02:42.180 --> 02:46.180
<b>July 8</b>

02:42.180 --> 02:47.680
<b>July 7</b>

02:42.180 --> 02:48.180
<b>Not available.</b>

02:42.680 --> 02:44.040
And in heat this bad,

02:43.430 --> 02:48.180
<b>July 6</b>

02:44.040 --> 02:48.180
it's probably gonna be hard to pencil 
in an install date anytime soon.

02:45.850 --> 02:48.180
<b>July 5</b>

02:48.180 --> 02:50.080
O-Oh, no...

02:50.080 --> 02:51.940
Oh, no worries there.

02:51.940 --> 02:54.440
I can install it!

02:54.440 --> 02:55.840
<i>Well, damn, dude.</i>

02:55.840 --> 02:57.940
<i>He really is reliable.</i>

02:58.220 --> 03:01.310
So let's go and buy that AC!

03:02.160 --> 03:03.700
<b>Multi-Camera Tokyo</b>

03:06.430 --> 03:09.200
There are all kinds of different 
air conditioners, huh?

03:09.200 --> 03:10.580
There sure are.

03:10.580 --> 03:16.840
CLEARANCE SALE!!

03:10.580 --> 03:16.840
CLEARANCE SALE!!

03:10.920 --> 03:13.200
The prices are totally different, too.

03:13.800 --> 03:16.840
I wonder how much of a 
functional difference there is.

03:17.150 --> 03:20.340
It's hard to know which one to 
pick with such a wide selection.

03:20.340 --> 03:25.220
<b>Trade-In
Discount
 Applicable</b>

03:20.640 --> 03:23.610
Excuse me, I'd like this one.

03:23.610 --> 03:26.350
Sure, let me just make sure it's in stock.

03:25.220 --> 03:26.350
So fast!

03:26.800 --> 03:29.680
I-Is it okay to decide so quickly 
without looking at all the options?

03:29.680 --> 03:31.680
Are you sure you don't want to compare a few?

03:31.680 --> 03:34.770
It's okay. I've got a good 
idea of how they work.

03:34.770 --> 03:36.980
How do you even know about that?!

03:37.460 --> 03:38.870
We do have it in stock.

03:38.870 --> 03:41.060
Can we get it delivered today?

03:41.060 --> 03:42.990
Sure, we can do that.

03:43.660 --> 03:46.140
It'll be delivered at 4:00 PM.

03:46.940 --> 03:48.640
That's kinda impressive...

03:48.640 --> 03:51.000
Seriously! We live in a convenient world.

03:51.000 --> 03:53.870
<b>Air Conditioning

Fans • Associated Products

Now on Sale</b>

03:51.350 --> 03:53.260
I was talking about you, darling.

03:53.260 --> 03:53.870
Huh?

03:56.210 --> 03:58.570
So, where to next?

03:58.570 --> 04:03.510
Well, you need some special gear to install 
an AC, so we're off to rent those.

04:03.510 --> 04:06.760
<b>Nakiri Technical</b>

04:05.030 --> 04:08.620
Here we are. This place belongs to 
someone I've known for a long time.

04:06.760 --> 04:09.270
<b>Nakiri <i>Technical</i></b>

04:10.360 --> 04:11.770
Hello there!

04:12.670 --> 04:13.520
Whoa.

04:14.480 --> 04:17.400
Well, look who it is. Hello there, Nasa-kun.

04:17.400 --> 04:20.210
Good to see you again, Nakiri-san.

04:20.210 --> 04:21.280
Likewise.

04:21.580 --> 04:24.050
<i>I-It's a young woman.</i>

04:24.530 --> 04:26.320
What brings you by today?

04:26.320 --> 04:29.690
I wanted to borrow the tools for 
installing an air conditioner.

04:29.690 --> 04:32.040
Yeah, with this sudden heat. Makes sense.

04:32.620 --> 04:37.040
Let's see, you'll need a 
vacuum pump, a duct cutter...

04:37.040 --> 04:38.980
Now, where are the flaring tools?

04:38.980 --> 04:42.800
U-Um, darling, how do you know her?

04:43.340 --> 04:45.430
That's Nakiri Ouka-san.

04:45.430 --> 04:47.180
We were classmates in middle school.

04:47.180 --> 04:49.900
What?! Then you're the same age?

04:49.900 --> 04:50.670
Yep.

04:51.290 --> 04:54.690
By the way, Nakiri-san, I got married!

04:54.690 --> 04:57.120
Oh, is that right?

04:57.120 --> 04:59.650
Is white an okay color for the slim duct?

04:59.860 --> 05:00.850
Sure.

05:00.850 --> 05:03.680
And this is my wife, Tsukasa-chan.

05:03.680 --> 05:06.280
I-It's nice to meet you. I'm Tsukasa.

05:06.650 --> 05:09.700
Yeah, I'm Nakiri Ouka. It's a pleasure.

05:10.060 --> 05:12.910
<i>She doesn't seem even mildly surprised.</i>

05:13.200 --> 05:16.560
That just leaves the hole saw and...

05:17.920 --> 05:20.150
Wait, you're married, Nasa-kun?!

05:20.150 --> 05:21.520
For real?! Since when?!

05:21.520 --> 05:22.420
Kinda slow...

05:22.770 --> 05:25.540
Well, it was fairly recently, to be honest.

05:25.540 --> 05:27.680
I bet! But you could've said something!

05:27.680 --> 05:30.880
It came as such a shock that 
it took a while to sink in!

05:30.880 --> 05:33.850
Sorry about that. It did come up kind of late...

05:33.850 --> 05:36.810
W-Well, regardless, congratulations.

05:37.390 --> 05:39.770
This isn't much, but...

05:39.770 --> 05:42.240
Have some sealant paste in lieu of a gift.

05:42.240 --> 05:44.440
Oh, hey, thanks!

05:45.000 --> 05:50.070
Still, to think that Nasa-kun is 
married now... That's a real shocker.

05:50.490 --> 05:52.260
Where did you even meet, anyway?

05:52.260 --> 05:53.180
On the street!

05:55.440 --> 05:58.090
I happened to catch a glimpse of her,

05:58.090 --> 06:00.080
and it was love at first sight.

06:00.340 --> 06:02.340
I-I see...

06:03.000 --> 06:06.000
To be honest, I figured you were like me.

06:06.000 --> 06:10.220
The type who'd never really have any 
interest in, or chance for, that sort of thing.

06:10.530 --> 06:14.470
Well, I can see how you 
would've thought that.

06:14.800 --> 06:18.630
I'm pretty sure if I hadn't met Tsukasa-chan,
 you would've been right.

06:19.660 --> 06:22.720
I was never all that concerned about romance.

06:22.720 --> 06:25.410
I don't think I ever will be again, either.

06:25.410 --> 06:29.860
I'm pretty sure my lifetime's worth of 
romantic love is all for Tsukasa-chan!

06:32.000 --> 06:33.870
I-I see...

06:34.340 --> 06:36.730
You never fail to impress.

06:38.170 --> 06:41.270
I-I'll waive your rental fees for today.

06:41.270 --> 06:43.980
Really?! Thanks!

06:45.540 --> 06:48.010
Okay, all installed.

06:50.810 --> 06:54.670
Wow, air conditioning really 
does make the place more comfy!

06:54.670 --> 06:56.140
Y-Yeah, it does.

06:58.800 --> 07:03.400
I'm pretty sure my lifetime's worth of 
romantic love is all for Tsukasa-chan!

07:05.460 --> 07:09.090
Since it's cooled down a bit, 
I think I'll raise the temperature.

07:09.680 --> 07:12.330
I-I'm still feeling warm, so maybe not.

07:12.330 --> 07:13.660
You sure?

07:13.900 --> 07:17.370
And since I'm sweaty, 
I'm gonna go take a bath.

07:17.370 --> 07:18.410
Okay.

07:29.640 --> 07:33.680
There's something really nice about a 
cool room after getting out the bath!

07:34.640 --> 07:36.680
<i>My wife is cute when enjoying cool air, too!</i>

07:37.520 --> 07:40.110
All right, Tsukasa-chan, 
how about we head to bed?

07:40.110 --> 07:40.850
Yeah.

07:43.880 --> 07:45.750
I'll turn everything off, then.

07:45.750 --> 07:48.060
Okay. Goodnight.

08:01.600 --> 08:02.710
Darling...

08:04.440 --> 08:05.710
What's wrong?

08:06.340 --> 08:09.630
Is it just me, or does turning off 
the AC before bed... make it hot?

08:09.630 --> 08:11.840
Oh, sorry! Were you having trouble sleeping?

08:11.840 --> 08:14.840
I wouldn't go that far, but...

08:15.100 --> 08:18.010
There's the feeling of going 
from a comfy room with the AC on

08:18.010 --> 08:21.610
to a room where summer is in full effect.

08:21.610 --> 08:25.240
How do I put this? It's like the 
contrast is making it hard to sleep.

08:25.240 --> 08:27.110
I-I see...

08:27.360 --> 08:30.980
In that case, why don't I set 
it to turn off in an hour?

08:30.980 --> 08:34.550
I think that's a brilliant idea, darling.

08:36.690 --> 08:37.680
Sleep tight.

08:37.680 --> 08:39.370
Goodnight.

08:46.780 --> 08:49.630
<i>Is it just me, or is it super cold now?</i>

08:50.420 --> 08:53.380
<i>Huh? What did I have the 
temperature set to, again?</i>

08:53.380 --> 08:58.640
<b>Remote</b>

08:53.380 --> 08:58.640
<b>Automatic</b>

08:53.380 --> 08:58.640
<b>Stop</b>

08:53.380 --> 08:58.640
<b>AC</b>

08:54.000 --> 08:56.430
<i>I think it was 26 degrees...</i>

08:56.430 --> 08:58.640
<i>Has 26 degrees always been this cold?</i>

08:59.070 --> 09:02.640
<i>Are newer model ACs this cold?</i>

09:03.010 --> 09:08.080
<i>Aw, man, I can't sleep! It's a hot night,
 but I'm too cold to sleep!</i>

09:08.080 --> 09:10.790
<i>And how is it that, when I'm this cold,</i>

09:10.790 --> 09:12.650
<i>Tsukasa-chan is totally...</i>

09:12.650 --> 09:17.780
<b>Brrr brrr</b>

09:12.980 --> 09:14.920
Darling, I'm cold.

09:14.920 --> 09:17.780
I know, right?! It really is, isn't it?!

09:18.120 --> 09:21.130
Maybe 26 degrees was too cold?

09:21.130 --> 09:22.540
I guess so.

09:22.540 --> 09:27.040
<b>Air Direction</b>

09:22.540 --> 09:27.040
<b>Up/Down</b>

09:22.540 --> 09:27.040
<b>Air Pressure</b>

09:22.880 --> 09:25.470
Let's set it to 28 degrees instead.

09:25.470 --> 09:28.790
Good idea. We can see how that works out.

09:32.310 --> 09:35.120
<i>This is pretty comfortable for me.</i>

09:35.120 --> 09:37.800
<i>I bet Tsukasa-chan will be 
able to sleep well now, too.</i>

09:44.170 --> 09:46.840
<i>Okay, she looks like she's super hot!</i>

09:47.310 --> 09:50.220
<i>Do girls run warmer than guys?</i>

09:51.120 --> 09:52.690
<i>Although, with that said...</i>

09:58.180 --> 10:00.080
<i>It's pretty nice.</i>

10:00.080 --> 10:00.950
<i>Wait, no!</i>

10:01.440 --> 10:03.780
<i>I'd hate for her to be uncomfortable.</i>

10:03.780 --> 10:06.460
<i>Let's set it to 27 degrees...</i>

10:07.690 --> 10:10.460
<i>And have the sleep timer 
turn it off in an hour.</i>

10:25.720 --> 10:29.730
<i>How are humans able to do that 
sort of thing unconsciously?</i>

10:30.210 --> 10:33.820
<i>This is a little chilly for me, but as 
long as Tsukasa-chan is comfortable.</i>

10:34.460 --> 10:36.010
<i>Goodnight...</i>

10:49.990 --> 10:52.830
Oh, sorry. Did I wake you?

10:52.830 --> 10:56.130
I woke up from the heat. Sorry.

10:57.550 --> 11:00.380
Let's leave the AC on a 
bit longer while we sleep.

11:00.380 --> 11:01.510
You sure?

11:01.880 --> 11:04.480
Well, newer models have 
better energy efficiency,

11:04.480 --> 11:07.390
and there's no point in having it 
if we're sitting around being hot.

11:08.290 --> 11:10.520
Thanks, darling.

11:10.960 --> 11:13.020
I like it to be comfy, too.

11:14.580 --> 11:15.600
I love you.

11:18.290 --> 11:20.070
Sleep well, darling.

11:20.070 --> 11:22.490
G-Goodnight...

11:24.720 --> 11:28.470
<i>After that, we both were a little 
too heated up to sleep.</i>

11:29.490 --> 11:33.020
<i>So we ended up setting the AC to 26.5.</i>

11:42.380 --> 11:43.440
Okay.

11:43.440 --> 11:45.220
Hey, Kaname.

11:45.550 --> 11:48.950
I wanted your help with something 
involving the summer festival.

11:48.950 --> 11:51.860
Shiba-san's asking me to help out.

11:51.860 --> 11:52.850
What do you think?

11:53.130 --> 11:56.000
I mean, I'd personally rather not, but...

11:56.000 --> 11:59.860
But you know how Shiba-san is. 
That could start another argument.

11:59.860 --> 12:01.610
Which is why I wanted to ask you...

12:01.610 --> 12:03.740
What should I do, Kaname?

12:05.490 --> 12:07.010
Wait, who are you?!

12:07.010 --> 12:08.740
I should be asking that!

12:09.370 --> 12:12.170
What are you doing here, 
lady?! You're not Kaname!

12:12.170 --> 12:16.000
I'm just a part-timer who's 
filling in for Kaname!

12:17.470 --> 12:21.010
Oh, huh. I see.

12:22.030 --> 12:25.760
This is rough. I could 
seriously use her advice.

12:26.760 --> 12:28.260
Okay, there's no other way.

12:29.100 --> 12:33.280
I'll just pretend you're Kaname and ask you!

12:33.280 --> 12:36.720
So, there's apparently a lot of trouble 
going into the summer festival...

12:36.720 --> 12:38.470
Okay, this isn't going to work!

12:38.470 --> 12:39.520
It's not?!

12:39.520 --> 12:40.650
Why would it?!

12:40.900 --> 12:45.820
Besides, would <i>you</i> be interested in 
hearing out a total stranger's problem?

12:46.260 --> 12:49.230
But don't you like helping people 
who seem to be in trouble?

12:49.230 --> 12:51.160
I don't think this falls under that category!

12:51.530 --> 12:54.920
For the record, I don't even know your name!

12:55.680 --> 12:56.480
My name?

12:56.480 --> 12:57.650
That's right!

12:57.650 --> 13:01.210
Come on, baby. Do we really need names?

13:01.210 --> 13:03.450
A friend in need is a friend indeed.

13:03.450 --> 13:05.680
You're the only one who needs something!

13:06.030 --> 13:08.850
Come on, don't sweat the details.

13:08.850 --> 13:10.350
Anyway, Shiba-san was asking me...

13:10.350 --> 13:13.060
Don't get into my personal space
like it's the natural thing to do!

13:13.390 --> 13:15.800
Who even is this Shiba-san person?!

13:15.800 --> 13:17.310
Because I have no idea!

13:17.310 --> 13:19.940
Wait, you've never heard of Shiba-san?!

13:19.940 --> 13:22.300
You know who I'm talking about! Come on!

13:22.300 --> 13:26.520
The Shiba-san who tends to be too reckless 
on Twitter and is always getting flamed.

13:26.520 --> 13:28.450
Well, I'm glad I don't know Shiba-san!

13:28.840 --> 13:30.210
Hey, Shiba-san's so bad!

13:30.210 --> 13:34.490
Just a little too righteous 
for these modern times!

13:34.490 --> 13:36.710
That's not making them sound any better!

13:36.710 --> 13:41.200
They just make a lot of political statements 
informed by heavily-biased news sources!

13:41.200 --> 13:43.460
This Shiba-san is sounding 
like serious bad news!

13:43.460 --> 13:46.330
And who even cares about them, anyway?!

13:46.330 --> 13:48.720
My point is that I can't
 help you with your issue!

13:52.780 --> 13:55.160
What if you put your hair up in pigtails?

13:55.740 --> 13:56.500
What?

13:56.500 --> 13:57.770
You've never heard of them?

13:57.770 --> 13:59.550
That's not what I meant.

13:59.550 --> 14:02.650
Why should I do my hair in pigtails?

14:02.650 --> 14:04.110
And this is a bathhouse.

14:04.500 --> 14:06.950
If you're not going to go in, 
then get out of here already.

14:06.950 --> 14:09.190
Let's table that for a minute.

14:09.190 --> 14:13.030
As you're already aware, I came 
here to ask for Kaname's advice.

14:13.030 --> 14:15.000
I wasn't exactly aware of that.

14:15.410 --> 14:17.600
But I'm quite a busy woman!

14:17.600 --> 14:20.880
Which is why I can't just loaf 
around here waiting for her!

14:21.200 --> 14:22.020
And?

14:22.020 --> 14:24.930
Y'know how she has her hair in pigtails?

14:24.930 --> 14:27.280
Maybe if you did your hair the same way,

14:27.280 --> 14:30.570
you'd be more willing to hear me out!

14:30.570 --> 14:32.640
What is going on in your brain?!

14:32.640 --> 14:33.920
Aw, no good?

14:33.920 --> 14:37.270
Absolutely not! I'm confused as 
to how you ever thought otherwise!

14:37.270 --> 14:39.910
I guess that's a no-go...

14:39.910 --> 14:43.010
<i>Seriously, what is with her?</i>

14:44.710 --> 14:45.780
<i>And now she's asleep.</i>

14:46.880 --> 14:48.780
<i>It's pretty clear she's a kid,</i>

14:49.430 --> 14:53.420
<i>but she's kinda... incredibly pretty.</i>

14:54.330 --> 14:56.330
Hey, it's Kyuuma-chan.

14:57.040 --> 14:59.230
Kaname-chan! Welcome home!

14:59.230 --> 15:01.420
Uh, I'm back, I guess.

15:01.670 --> 15:02.960
Kyuuma-chan?

15:02.960 --> 15:06.300
This is Kagami Kyuuma-chan. 
A classmate of mine.

15:06.300 --> 15:09.930
Where the heck have you 
been, Kaname? I was waiting!

15:09.930 --> 15:12.400
Uh, I was at school, Kyuuma-chan.

15:12.400 --> 15:13.980
Huh? School?

15:13.980 --> 15:17.970
Exactly. Why weren't you there, by the way?

15:17.970 --> 15:22.310
Uh, well, I'm just... k-kinda stupid, so...

15:22.310 --> 15:23.810
That I knew.

15:24.060 --> 15:26.450
Wait, we had class today?!

15:26.450 --> 15:30.000
You should've told me! I had 
perfect attendance before!

15:30.000 --> 15:32.070
Why did you think it was a day off, anyway?

15:32.070 --> 15:35.440
Because everyone in class was 
talking about summer break.

15:35.440 --> 15:37.140
I thought it had started already.

15:37.140 --> 15:38.740
Is this girl gonna be okay?

15:38.740 --> 15:40.830
Not even a little bit, no.

15:41.060 --> 15:43.920
Kyuuma-chan here is dumber than 
most people think is possible,

15:43.920 --> 15:45.760
so I worry about her a lot.

15:45.760 --> 15:48.340
Aw, don't try and flatter me!

15:48.340 --> 15:50.470
That wasn't any kind of flattery, Kyuuma-chan!

15:51.690 --> 15:53.640
So, what did you need?

15:53.640 --> 15:56.250
Oh, I actually needed to ask for 
your advice about something...

15:56.250 --> 15:59.280
Wait, did you just call me dumb?!

15:59.280 --> 16:01.050
Who are you calling dumb?!

16:01.050 --> 16:03.180
<i>This is going nowhere fast.</i>

16:03.180 --> 16:04.230
Huh?

16:04.230 --> 16:07.250
I thought I heard a plucky voice.

16:07.250 --> 16:08.730
It's Kyuuma-chan!

16:08.730 --> 16:11.280
Hey, Yuzaki-paisen! It's been a while.

16:11.280 --> 16:12.580
It sure has.

16:12.580 --> 16:14.610
You're as energetic as ever.

16:15.040 --> 16:17.180
Welcome home, darling.

16:17.180 --> 16:18.120
I'm back.

16:18.380 --> 16:19.120
Huh?

16:19.370 --> 16:22.000
Yuzaki-paisen, when you say you're back...

16:22.000 --> 16:25.680
Yeah, I've been actually staying 
here at Kaname-chan's place.

16:25.680 --> 16:26.870
You have?

16:26.870 --> 16:27.500
Yep.

16:27.830 --> 16:31.010
And while I'm updating you, I got married.

16:32.760 --> 16:35.130
You married Kaname, Paisen?!

16:35.130 --> 16:37.200
No, Kyuuma-chan.

16:37.200 --> 16:40.890
Did you not notice the person 
that called him "darling"?

16:41.420 --> 16:44.730
This is my wife, Yuzaki Tsukasa-san.

16:44.730 --> 16:45.900
Nice to meet you.

16:46.650 --> 16:50.060
So that's why you called him "darling"?!

16:50.060 --> 16:51.780
So you <i>did</i> hear that?

16:51.780 --> 16:55.910
How did you get the idea that I was the 
one married to Senpai, in that case?

16:56.160 --> 16:58.550
I see! Well, ain't that something?

16:58.550 --> 17:02.280
It's a real shock, but congratulations.

17:02.280 --> 17:03.290
Thanks.

17:03.730 --> 17:08.690
Well, Tsukasa-chan, I need to return 
the tools I borrowed from Nakiri-san.

17:08.690 --> 17:12.230
Okay. Tell her I said thanks.

17:12.230 --> 17:14.020
Got it. I will.

17:14.020 --> 17:15.930
Have a safe trip.

17:15.930 --> 17:20.680
<b>Bath Tickets</b>

17:17.610 --> 17:20.680
To think that Yuzaki-paisen got married...

17:20.970 --> 17:26.690
Well, I still don't get much about 
romance at all, much less marriage.

17:26.960 --> 17:29.830
Do you smooch and stuff when you get married?

17:30.740 --> 17:34.290
Well, it's not like we don't, but...

17:34.290 --> 17:35.200
But what?

17:35.810 --> 17:37.970
How many times in a day?

17:37.970 --> 17:39.900
Who usually initiates?

17:40.620 --> 17:42.660
When did you last kiss?

17:43.130 --> 17:44.530
When you kiss—

17:44.530 --> 17:47.710
Okay, pipe down! I'm not 
playing 20 questions with you!

17:47.710 --> 17:51.180
Besides, I thought you were 
here to talk to Kaname!

17:51.180 --> 17:52.960
So talk to her already!

17:52.960 --> 17:55.640
Oh, right, I forgot about that.

17:55.640 --> 17:58.540
Kaname, I need some advice on something!

17:58.540 --> 17:59.340
What?

18:02.280 --> 18:03.850
I dunno, though...

18:03.850 --> 18:05.190
What is it?

18:05.190 --> 18:09.350
I mean, I did want to get your advice.

18:09.700 --> 18:10.860
But Häagen...

18:10.860 --> 18:11.860
Häagen?

18:12.260 --> 18:15.860
I don't think I'm gonna 
talk without any Häagen.

18:19.650 --> 18:21.380
You're the one asking her for advice!

18:21.380 --> 18:23.260
Where does ice cream even enter into it?!

18:23.260 --> 18:27.060
And Häagen?! Trying to get the 
good stuff while you're at it?!

18:28.620 --> 18:33.200
B-But problems like this are always 
better with a tasty snack...

18:33.200 --> 18:36.880
I don't even know what problem 
it is yet, so just ask!

18:38.100 --> 18:40.260
Then will you buy me 
the ice cream afterward?

18:40.260 --> 18:42.160
Sure, whatever, okay?!

18:42.160 --> 18:43.640
I dunno, though...

18:43.640 --> 18:46.140
You don't even care anymore, do you?!

18:46.520 --> 18:48.320
Okay, I've made up my mind!

18:48.320 --> 18:52.360
I think I'm gonna go grab that Häagen, 
and then I'll be back for advice!

18:53.400 --> 18:55.600
So I'll catch you later, Kaname!

18:55.600 --> 18:58.650
Wait, hold on, Kyuuma-chan!

18:59.690 --> 19:01.760
She's an odd girl.

19:01.760 --> 19:02.660
Yeah.

19:02.950 --> 19:04.640
The thing is...

19:04.640 --> 19:06.250
As crazy as she is,

19:06.250 --> 19:09.660
and as impossible as it is to understand 
anything she says or does...

19:09.660 --> 19:12.460
Kaname! Hey, Kaname! What flavor do you want?

19:12.460 --> 19:14.420
S-Strawberry, then.

19:14.420 --> 19:16.520
'Kay! Consider it done!

19:20.210 --> 19:21.180
So there you have it...

19:21.770 --> 19:24.850
She's just really cute, y'know?

19:24.850 --> 19:26.360
I see.

19:28.950 --> 19:31.940
Nakiri-san! Thanks a bunch for the tools.

19:32.290 --> 19:35.380
Hey. Did the installation go well?

19:35.380 --> 19:36.320
Yep!

19:36.640 --> 19:38.400
Pretty smoothly, I guess.

19:38.400 --> 19:40.320
That's good to hear.

19:40.670 --> 19:45.560
I'm still having trouble believing 
you got married, Nasa-kun.

19:46.550 --> 19:49.850
I don't really have a desire to,
 so it's hard to picture.

19:50.380 --> 19:53.690
Is being married a good thing?

19:53.690 --> 19:56.210
Well, it probably depends on the person.

19:56.720 --> 19:59.520
But I think it's pretty good.

19:59.520 --> 20:02.840
I-I see. In what ways?

20:02.840 --> 20:06.670
Well, let's see. For one thing...

20:06.670 --> 20:09.350
My wife always smells great!

20:10.310 --> 20:11.480
She does?!

20:11.480 --> 20:14.730
Yeah! It's really pretty incredible!

20:15.160 --> 20:17.320
When we walk together at night,

20:17.320 --> 20:20.280
I always end up standing downwind.

20:20.280 --> 20:24.740
And there's this sweet scent, 
like I'm in a field of flowers!

20:25.280 --> 20:28.660
Sometimes I feel like I'm gonna go crazy!

20:28.660 --> 20:30.620
W-Well, that is certainly...

20:30.940 --> 20:33.390
I think it may be a bit advanced for me.

20:33.920 --> 20:35.230
Anything else come to mind?

20:36.120 --> 20:37.500
Oh, right!

20:37.500 --> 20:39.430
Nakiri-san, did you know that girls

20:39.430 --> 20:43.710
will buy cookies based on 
the design of the package?

20:43.710 --> 20:45.260
Th-That's crazy!

20:45.700 --> 20:47.510
Who even does that?!

20:47.510 --> 20:49.920
Shouldn't you buy cookies 
based on their flavor?!

20:49.920 --> 20:52.520
I was surprised at first, too.

20:52.880 --> 20:56.520
I asked her, "Shouldn't you pick 
food based on how it tastes?"

20:56.790 --> 20:59.340
But then, she told me...

20:59.340 --> 21:01.510
Well, of course the taste matters,

21:01.510 --> 21:03.780
but the cuteness of the 
packaging matters, too.

21:04.080 --> 21:06.570
Besides, if they put 
effort into the package,

21:06.570 --> 21:09.000
they're bound to put it into the taste, too.

21:09.000 --> 21:11.160
And if the box is cute,

21:11.620 --> 21:14.370
it makes you more excited 
when you pick it up, right?

21:15.510 --> 21:19.460
She does have a point there, I think.

21:19.460 --> 21:22.280
It's like how I get excited 
about a rotary engine,

21:22.280 --> 21:26.470
and start thinking if I get 
a car, it's gotta be an RX-7.

21:26.470 --> 21:27.680
It's the same thing!

21:27.680 --> 21:30.000
Girls buy cookies based on the packaging...

21:30.000 --> 21:32.220
This is pretty educational! Anything else?

21:32.220 --> 21:34.850
Well, do you know about this?

21:35.760 --> 21:36.850
Girls...

21:39.170 --> 21:41.980
tend to prefer to drink warm water.

21:41.980 --> 21:44.360
W-Warm water?!

21:44.360 --> 21:46.810
Th-That sounds like room 
temperature nonsense!

21:46.810 --> 21:50.140
Everyone knows the best drinks 
are the ice cold ones!

21:51.170 --> 21:52.870
Apparently not, actually!

21:53.310 --> 21:54.810
According to my wife...

21:54.810 --> 21:56.120
Here, Tsukasa-chan.

21:56.480 --> 21:57.370
No thanks.

21:57.370 --> 22:01.880
If you drink that cold stuff all 
the time, you'll catch a chill.

22:02.240 --> 22:03.830
Listen closely, Nakiri-san!

22:03.830 --> 22:06.370
By drinking warm water intentionally,

22:06.370 --> 22:10.570
girls are trying to avoid feeling cold!
 And they do it on purpose!

22:10.570 --> 22:12.890
Do you understand how 
delicate that makes them?!

22:13.650 --> 22:15.820
I-I had no idea.

22:16.670 --> 22:19.440
There's a lot to learn about girls.

22:19.440 --> 22:20.690
There sure is!

22:21.030 --> 22:25.940
But the best thing about getting married, 
to me, is how my world has expanded.

22:26.460 --> 22:27.650
The world?

22:27.650 --> 22:28.320
Right!

22:28.660 --> 22:30.520
By living together,

22:30.520 --> 22:34.080
I'm discovering things every day 
that I had no idea about.

22:34.870 --> 22:38.370
I go to places I've never been before, think 
about things I never considered before,

22:38.740 --> 22:40.380
experience emotions I've never felt,

22:40.700 --> 22:42.880
meet people I wouldn't have met otherwise...

22:43.280 --> 22:46.000
All of those things combined

22:46.000 --> 22:49.130
have made me feel like I have 
more potential than before.

22:50.480 --> 22:53.690
It feels like the world itself is bigger.

23:02.790 --> 23:06.150
Well, Nakiri-san, I'll be seeing you!

23:06.420 --> 23:08.050
Sure. Until next time.

23:12.090 --> 23:15.440
<i>Your world expanding by meeting new people...</i>

23:18.280 --> 23:19.410
<i>Maybe I...</i>

23:20.500 --> 23:22.890
<i>should look for a wife, too.</i>

23:24.920 --> 23:39.930
<b>Next Episode Preview</b>

23:25.520 --> 23:27.300
Life is a sauna!

23:27.300 --> 23:30.050
Great, my sister's lost her marbles again.

23:30.050 --> 23:32.050
There are times when people 
must show restraint.

23:32.050 --> 23:35.380
You oughta make that your phone's wallpaper 
and re-read it a hundred times over.

23:35.380 --> 23:38.450
Which is why I will restrain myself by
giving up on this gacha some other time!

23:38.450 --> 23:39.930
Okay, we're done here!
